+# Bug Assessment: Product review privacy, validation, and aggregates
+
+- **Slug**: ticket
+- **Created**: 2026-11-18T00:00:00+00:00
+- **Source**: pasted text
+- **Verdict**: valid
+- **Severity**: high
+
+## Report (verbatim or summarized)
+
+A customer reported that public product reviews expose the reviewer's email and home address. Support also found that a second review by the same customer returns a server error, rating 9 returns a server error, and merchant edits/deletes do not update the product rating. The requested behavior is privacy-safe public output, 1–5 whole-number validation with 400, duplicate reviews with 409, customer identity mismatch with 403, product-scoped merchant update/delete with 404 for missing or mismatched reviews, and accurate one-decimal half-up product aggregates after every change.
+
+## Symptom
+
+`GET /api/v1/product/{id}/reviews` serializes a full `ReadableCustomer`, including email and billing/delivery data. Review creation maps duplicate and out-of-range conditions to 500/503, does not authenticate the submitted customer id, and validation accepts fractional ratings. Review persistence increments the aggregate for updates and deletion does not recalculate it.
+
+## Reproduction
+
+1. Create a product review, then request `GET /api/v1/product/{id}/reviews` and inspect the customer fields.
+2. Post a second review for the same customer and product; post a rating of 9.
+3. Post a review using a different customer's id from the authenticated customer.
+4. Update or delete a review through `/api/v1/private/products/{id}/reviews/{reviewId}` and request `GET /api/v2/product/{sku}`.
+
+## Suspected Code Paths
+
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/api/v1/product/ProductReviewApi.java` — review endpoints catch all exceptions and send 500/503; duplicate and rating checks use incorrect statuses; the update path does not verify the URL product; the authenticated principal is not checked.
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/populator/catalog/ReadableProductReviewPopulator.java` — populates the public review's customer using `ReadableCustomerPopulator`.
+- `sm-shop-model/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/model/catalog/product/ReadableProductReview.java` — public DTO exposes a full customer object.
+- `sm-shop-model/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/model/catalog/product/ProductReviewEntity.java` — rating has range validation but accepts fractional values and uses `Double`.
+- `sm-core/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/core/business/services/catalog/product/review/ProductReviewServiceImpl.java` — aggregate calculation always adds a rating and increments count, including updates.
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/facade/product/ProductCommonFacadeImpl.java` — delete delegates directly to the review service without aggregate recalculation.
+- `sm-core/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/core/business/repositories/catalog/product/review/ProductReviewRepository.java` — review lookup supports duplicate detection and product/customer loading.
+
+## Root Cause Hypothesis
+
+Confidence: high. The public populator deliberately delegates to a broad customer populator, while the review service treats every save as a new review and never derives aggregates from the current review set. The controller's manual error handling converts business failures to server errors and lacks authenticated-customer and URL-product authorization checks. The DTO constraints do not constrain the rating's fractional part.
+
+## Proposed Remediation
+
+**Preferred**: Replace the public review customer payload with a deliberately minimal reviewer representation containing only the reviewer's first name, while retaining only review id, rating, description, date, and language as appropriate for the review contract. Add whole-number rating validation and explicit controller responses for 400, 403, 404, and 409. For customer-authenticated creation, compare the request customer's id with the authenticated `JWTUser` id before doing any persistence and set/check the URL product id before duplicate detection.
+
+Make review aggregate maintenance derive count and average from the product's current reviews after create, update, and delete. Recalculate from the repository, round with `RoundingMode.HALF_UP` to one decimal place, and set zero values when no reviews remain. Ensure update and delete reject reviews belonging to a different URL product with 404.
+
+**Files likely to change**:
+
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/api/v1/product/ProductReviewApi.java`
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/populator/catalog/ReadableProductReviewPopulator.java`
+- `sm-shop-model/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/model/catalog/product/ReadableProductReview.java`
+- `sm-shop-model/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/model/catalog/product/ProductReviewEntity.java`
+- `sm-core/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/core/business/services/catalog/product/review/ProductReviewServiceImpl.java`
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/facade/product/ProductCommonFacadeImpl.java`
+- `sm-core/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/core/business/repositories/catalog/product/review/ProductReviewRepository.java`
+
+**Tests to add or update**:
+
+- Endpoint tests for privacy-safe fields, rating boundaries and fractional ratings, duplicate conflict, authenticated-customer mismatch, and product-scoped update/delete status codes.
+- Service/API tests proving aggregate average/count after create, edit, delete, and deleting the final review, including half-up rounding.
+
+## Risks & Considerations
+
+- Removing fields from the public review JSON is an intentional security/privacy API change.
+- Existing data may contain fractional or out-of-range ratings; recalculation should use the stored values without allowing new invalid input.
+- Repository-derived recalculation adds a read after writes but guarantees correctness for update/delete and stale aggregates.
+- Direct `sendError` handling can commit an incorrect response before the global REST exception handler; endpoint control flow should return explicit statuses or throw mapped exceptions.
+
+## Open Questions
+
+- [NEEDS CLARIFICATION: The repository has no obvious end-to-end fixture for authenticated product-review requests, so full HTTP verification may require application/database setup.]
